  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Status / findings\n\n**Works, verified.** Task 0 gate: Matteo's `BaxOp` at $\\varphi=0$ reduces *identically* to our\n`gaudinODE` (15 equations, one branch, residual 0, symbolic in $S,P,\\mu,w_1,w_2$), giving the\n$h\\leftrightarrow$Casimir dictionary. Staggering $d_k-M_k=\\{0,1,2,3\\}$ verified, and\n$\\deg Q_k^{(n)}\\le d_k+n$ across all orders tested. For $\\mu=\\{2,1,1,0\\}$ at $(S,P)=(1,1)$: solved\nto order $\\varepsilon^4$, unique at every order, twisted residual vanishes through order 4 on all\nfour branches, and **all nine $h^{(n)}$ agree with Matteo's exact solve at every order 0-4**.\nOrder-0 Wronskian is exactly $768\\,z^{2S}(z-1)^{2P}$, matching Abel's formula -- an independent\ncheck on `GaudinSolve` itself.\n\n**The obstruction.** Order-by-order does *not* close for all $\\mu$. Measured residual freedom at\norder 1, after removing the $L_0$-kernel gauge:\n\n| $\\mu$ | free params | moves $h$? |\n|---|---|---|\n| $\\{2,2,0,0\\},\\{1,1,1,1\\},\\{3,3,0,0\\},\\{2,2,1,1\\},\\{4,4,0,0\\},\\{3,3,1,1\\},\\{2,2,2,2\\}$ | 0 | pure gauge |\n| $\\{2,1,1,0\\},\\{4,2,2,0\\},\\{3,2,2,1\\}$ | 1 | yes |\n| $\\{3,2,1,0\\},\\{4,3,1,0\\}$ | 2 | yes |\n\nEmpirically **free $=(\\#\\text{distinct values of }\\mu)-2$**, floored at 0: it vanishes exactly for\nthe paired weights $\\mu_1=\\mu_2,\\ \\mu_3=\\mu_4$ and grows with how generic $\\mu$ is.\n\nThe freedom is *not* frame convention -- for $\\mu=\\{3,2,1,0\\}$ a single choice\n($aa[1,1]=-\\psi_1$, $aa[2,1]=472/405$ at $\\psi=\\{1,\\tfrac13,\\tfrac15,\\tfrac17\\}$) reproduces all\nnine of Matteo's exact $h^{(1)}$, a 9-equation/2-unknown overdetermined match. The Baxter equation\nat that order simply does not know it.\n\n**Two routes ruled out.**\n- *Matteo's rigid monic ansatz.* It does fix the freedom, but only because it is singular at\n  $\\varphi=0$: measured pole orders of $cc[k,j]$ are exactly $M_k-j$ ($cc[4,0]\\sim\\varepsilon^{-3}$,\n  $cc[4,1]\\sim\\varepsilon^{-2}$, $cc[4,2]\\sim\\varepsilon^{-1}$, ...). Excluded by the regular-Q\n  requirement.\n- *Wronskian / Abel.* Fully absorbed by the $\\varepsilon$-dependent overall constant; constrains\n  nothing. It is a consequence of the Baxter equation, so it cannot supply missing information.\n\n**Where the missing data lives.** At $\\varphi=0$ all four exponentials $e^{-\\varphi_k z}$ coincide,\nso the untwisted solution carries no record of which branch is which. The natural resolution is the\nconfluent / divided-difference basis: $(e^{-\\varphi_2 z}-e^{-\\varphi_1 z})/(\\varphi_1-\\varphi_2)\\to\nz\\,e^{-\\varphi z}$ raises the polynomial degree by exactly one per confluence step, reproducing\n$d_k=M_k+(k-1)$. Branch 1 is the $k=1$ case of this ($d_1=M_1$, no divided difference needed),\nwhich is why imposing $Q_1=e^{-\\varphi_1 z}P_1$ supplies exactly one unit of the missing data --\nenough for $\\mu$ with 3 distinct values, not enough for 4.\n\n**Not started:** dual sector $Q^\\dagger$ (dual Baxter + Hodge cross-check).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
